  "abstract_summary": "A frequent claim in real-time object detection is that non-maximum suppression (NMS) removes true objects when they touch, so that NMS-free detectors are needed in crowded scenes. We test this claim in snooker, where the geometry is known exactly: spheres of diameter 52.5 mm on a table of known size, including fifte...",
